<title>SPAIN: Spain Q1 GDP up 2.9 pct yr/yr, up 0.9 pct qtr/qtr.</title>
<headline>Spain Q1 GDP up 2.9 pct yr/yr, up 0.9 pct qtr/qtr.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute</p>
<p>gave the following figures, 1986 prices (pct change, revised</p>
<p>figures marked &quot;R&quot;):</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	    Q1 '97   Q4 '96  Q197 VS Q496</p>
<p>					    yr/yr    yr/yr	qtr/qtr</p>
<p> Gross domestic product	     2.9	2.6	   0.9</p>
<p> Private consumption		  2.8	2.4 R	 1.0</p>
<p> Public sector consumption	 -1.5     -1.1 R	-0.2</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	    Q1 '97   Q4 '96  Q197 VS Q496</p>
<p>					    yr/yr    yr/yr	qtr/qtr</p>
<p> Gross fixed capital formation    1.4	 0.0R	 1.4</p>
<p>    Capital goods		     7.8	 7.7R	 2.5</p>
<p>    Construction		     -2.3	-4.2R	 0.7</p>
<p> Variation in stocks		 -0.2	 0.0R	 n.a.</p>
<p> Internal demand			1.6	 1.3R	 0.8</p>
<p> Exports				 11.2	13.2R	 1.4</p>
<p> Imports				  6.4	 8.2R	 1.0</p>
</text>
